          %p
            Here for
            = succeed "-supersymmetry" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 5
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5 \leq \mathcal{N} \leq 8
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            is via the canonical action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            as in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            (
            %a{:href => "#MedeirosFigueroa10"}> Medeiros-Figueroa 10
            ), while for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 4
            then there is an extra twist to the action (
            %a{:href => "#MFFGME09"}> MFFGME 09
            ). See the table
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#WorldvolumeTheory"} below
          %h4#BlackM2BranesInThePresenceOfG4Flux In the presence of 4-flux
          %p
            In the presence of non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            is not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7 \coloneqq \star G_4
            alone, but receives corrections, first due to the quadratic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            self-interaction in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            expected in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
              literature
            states the corrected 7-flux to be the following combination, also known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Page+charge"} Page charge
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Page83"} Page 83 (8)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DuffStelle91"} Duff-Stelle 91 (43)
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#BaggerLambertMukhiPapageorgakis13"} BLMP 13, p. 21
          #eq:FirstCorrectionToG7.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ˜
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widetilde G'_7
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  G_7 + \tfrac{1}{2} C_3 \wedge G_4
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the second term subtracts the electric flux induced by the self-intersection of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+differential+form"} closed differential form
            if the naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            hold:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \widetilde G_7
                  \\;=\;
                  0
                  \\,.
          %p
            But in fact
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FirstCorrectionToG7"} (1)
            does not quite make general sense, for two reasons:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                In general
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4 = 0
                is not an admissible condition and is not the actual vanshing of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            %li
              %p
                Even if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
                happens to be integrally quantizaed (if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 4
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{4}p_1
                is integral) the appearance of a globally defined
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                potential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3
                in
                = succeed ",means" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FirstCorrectionToG7"} (1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
                actually does vanish after all.
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong
              Charge-quantized
              = succeed "-flux" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi G
                          %mo ˜
                        %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde G_7
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS 19b, Prop. 4.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS19c"} FSS 19c, Section 4
          %p
            Both of these issues are solved if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            is taken to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} charge quantized
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ). This gives the corrected formula
          #eq:FullCorrectionToG7.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
