          %h2#References References
          %ul
            %li#Duff99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              , chapter 2 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"} ISBN:9780750306720
          %div
            %h3#SuperMembraneAsSigmaModelReferences Super-membrane/M2-brane as a sigma model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma-model"} Green-Schwarz sigma-model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membrane"} super-membrane
              in 11d (as in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
              and in contrast to the
              = succeed "-solutions" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %ul
              %li#BergshoeffSezginTownsend87
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Bergshoeff"}> Eric Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supermembranes and eleven-dimensional supergravity
                %strong 189
                (1987) 75-78 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91272-X"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91272-X
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/248230/"} spire:248230
            %p
              Via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superembedding+approach"} superembedding approach
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
              were obtained in
            %ul
              %li#BPSTV95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Pasti"} Paolo Pasti
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Sorokin"} Dmitri Sorokin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mario+Tonin"} Mario Tonin
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Volkov"} Dmitry Volkov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superstrings and supermembranes in the doubly supersymmetric geometrical approach
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501113"} arXiv:hep-th/9501113
            %p
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              in:
            %ul
              %li#HoweSezgin05
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"}> Paul Howe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The supermembrane revisited
                %strong 22
                (2005) 2167-2200 [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412245"}> arXiv:hep-th/0412245
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/22/11/017"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/22/11/017
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
              of the M2-brane to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
              was observed in
            %ul
              %li#DuffHoweInamiStelle87
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"}> Michael Duff
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Howe"} Paul Howe
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Superstrings in
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo =
                            %mn 10
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=10
                      from Supermembranes in
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi D
                            %mo =
                            %mn 11
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
                  %strong 191
                  (1987) 70 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2"}> doi:10.1016/0370-2693(87)91323-2
                  ]
                %p
                  also in:
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Duff"} Michael Duff
                  (ed.):
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"} The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  205-206 (1987) [
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245249"}> spire:245249
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"}> Paul Townsend
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em The eleven-dimensional supermembrane revisited
                  %strong 350
                  (1995) 184-187 [
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9501068"}> arXiv:hep-th/9501068
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(95)00397-4
            %p
              around the time when
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              became accepted due to
            %ul
              %li#Witten95
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+Theory+Dynamics+In+Various+Dimensions"} String Theory Dynamics In Various Dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9503124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9503124
                )
            %p On the early history of these developments:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+A.+Bergshoeff"}> Eric A. Bergshoeff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ergin+Sezgin"} Ergin Sezgin
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+K.+Townsend"} Paul K. Townsend
                %em A brief history of supermembranes
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.06234"}> arXiv:2503.06234
                ]
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Bandos"}> Igor Bandos
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
                  %em SDiff Gauge Theory and the M2 Condensate
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1583"}> arXiv:0808.1583
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maria+P.+Garcia+del+Moral"}> Maria P. Garcia del Moral
                  , C. Las Heras, P. Leon, J. M. Pena,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alvaro+Restuccia"} Alvaro Restuccia
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Fluxes, Twisted tori, Monodromy and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
                      Supermembranes
                  %strong 2020
                  97 (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.06397"}> arXiv:2005.06397
                  ,
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP09(2020)097"} doi:10.1007/JHEP09(2020)097
            %p
              Discussion from the point of view of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Wess-Zumino-Witten+theory"} ∞-Wess-Zumino-Witten theory
            %ul
              %li#FSS2013
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super p-branes with tensor multiplet fields
                (2013)
            %p
              On possible structures in M2-brane dynamics and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-M5-brane+bound+states"} M2-M5-brane bound states
              which could be
              = succeed "-lifts" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+system"} integrability
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS+spacetime"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi AdS
                        %mn 5
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_5
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5-sphere"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 5
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^5
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirill+Gubarev"}> Kirill Gubarev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edvard+Musaev"} Edvard Musaev
                %em Integrability structures in string theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.06486"}> arXiv:2301.06486
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %div
            %h3#LightConeQuantizationOfM2BranesToBFSSMatrixModel Quantization of the M2-brane sigma-model to a matrix model
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-formulation" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mechanics"} classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge"} light-cone gauge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
              for the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativistic+membrane"} relativistic membrane
              and the corresponding matrix
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutator"} commutator
              regularization is due to:
            %ul
              %li#Hoppe82
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum theory of a massless relativistic surface and a two-dimensional bound state problem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1721.1/15717"} dspace:1721.1/15717
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HoppeMembrane82.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %p Some exact solutions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em Exact algebraic M(em)brane solutions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.00569"} arXiv:2107.00569
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Hoppe"}> Jens Hoppe
                  ,
                  %em The fast non-commutative sharp drop
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.13146"} arXiv:2302.13146
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              On the regularized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge+quantization"} light-cone gauge quantization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+model"} Green-Schwarz sigma model
              for the
