            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                So Katagiri:
                %em A Lorentz Covariant Matrix Model for Bosonic M2-Branes: Nambu Brackets and Restricted Volume-Preserving Deformations
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.05940"}> arXiv2504.05940
                ]
          %h3#ReferencesAsABlackBrane As a black brane
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            membrane solution of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            was found in
          %ul
            %li#DuffStelle91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Multi-membrane solutions of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo =
                        %mn 11
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 11
                  supergravity
              %strong 253
              1-2 (1991) 113-118 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/299386"}> spire:299386
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-2693(91)91371-2"} doi:10.1016/0370-2693(91)91371-2
          %p
            Its regularity across the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizon"} event horizon
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#DuffGibbonsTownsend94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"} Gary Gibbons
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Townsend"} Paul Townsend
              = succeed "," do
                %em Macroscopic superstrings as interpolating solitons
              %strong 332
              (1994) 321-328 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9405124"}> arXiv:hep-th/9405124
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Further discussion of such
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freund-Rubin+compactifications"} Freund-Rubin compactifications
          %ul
            %li#Page83
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Don+Page"}> Don Page
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Classical stability of round and squashed seven-spheres in eleven-dimensional supergravity
              %strong 28
              12 (1983) 2976-2982 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/14480"}> spire:14480
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.28.2976"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.28.2976
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Horava-Witten+theory"} Horava-Witten
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifold"} orientifold
            of the black M2, supposedly yielding the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#LalakLukasOvrut97
              %p
                Zygmunt Lalak, André Lukas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burt+Ovrut"} Burt Ovrut
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Soliton Solutions of M-theory on an Orbifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9709214"} arXiv:hep-th/9709214
            %li#Kashima00
              %p
                Ken Kashima,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The M2-brane Solution of Heterotic M-theory with the Gauss-Bonnet
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi R
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^2
                    terms
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0010286"} arXiv:hep-th/0010286
          %p
            Meanwhile
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            was recognized in
          %ul
            %li#Maldacena97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"}> Juan Maldacena
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Large N limit of superconformal field theories and supergravity
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711200"} hep-th/9711200
          %p
            where a dual description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            theory of M2-brane appears in section 3.2. More on this is in
          %ul
            %li#KlebanovTorri10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Klebanov"}> Igor Klebanov
              , Giuseppe Torri,
              = succeed "," do
                %em M2-branes and AdS/CFT
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.1580"} arXiv:0909.1580
          %p An account of the history as of 1999 is in
          %ul
            %li#Duff99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              , chapter II of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+World+in+Eleven+Dimensions"}> The World in Eleven Dimensions
                  \: Supergravity, Supermembranes and M-theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.crcpress.com/The-World-in-Eleven-Dimensions-Supergravity-supermembranes-and-M-theory/Duff/9780750306720"} publisher
          %p More recent review is in
          %ul
            %li
              Georgios Linardopoulos, chapter 13 of
              %em Classical Strings and Membranes in the AdS/CFT Correspondence
              (
              %a{:href => "http://users.uoa.gr/~glinardo/Thesis.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/1391031/"} spire
          %p
            A detailed discussion of this
            = succeed "-realization" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            and its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT"} AdS-CFT
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gianguido+Dall%27Agata"}> Gianguido Dall'Agata
              , Davide FabbKri, Christophe Fraser,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Fr%C3%A9"} Pietro Fré
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  The
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Osp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 8
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Osp(8|4)
                  singleton action from the supermembrane
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9807115"} arXiv:hep-th/9807115
          %p
            The generalization of this to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 1/2
            BPS sugra solutions of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4 \times X_7
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#MFFGME09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sunil+Gadhia"} Sunil Gadhia
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elena+M%C3%A9ndez-Escobar"} Elena Méndez-Escobar
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Half-BPS quotients in M-theory: ADE with a twist
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.0163"} arXiv:0909.0163
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~jmf/CV/Seminars/YRM2010.pdf"} pdf slides
            %li#MedeirosFigueroa10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+de+Medeiros"}> Paul de Medeiros
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Figueroa-O%27Farrill"} José Figueroa-O'Farrill
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Half-BPS M2-brane orbifolds
                %strong 16
                5 (2012) 1349-1408 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.4761"}> arXiv:1007.4761
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.atmp/1408561553"} euclid:atmp/1408561553
          %p Further solutions:
          %ul
            %li
              A. M. Ghezelbash,
              %em M-Branes on Minimal Surfaces
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.07855"}> arXiv:2407.07855
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Fridrik Freyr Gautason, Jesse van Muiden:
                %em Localisation of the M2-brane
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16597"}> arXiv:2503.16597
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Alex Buchel, Ruben Monten:
                %em Near-extremal membranes in M-theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.01974"}> arXiv:2511.01974
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#in_
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi AdS
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi CFT
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_4/CFT_3
          %p
            In
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS4-CFT3+duality"} AdS4-CFT3 duality
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              Kazuo Hosomichi,
              %em M2-branes and AdS/CFT: A Review
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.13914"}> arXiv:2003.13914
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#history History
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"}> Mike Duff
              \:
              %p
                %em M-history without the M
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1501.04098"}> arXiv:1501.04098
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#decoupled_worldvolume_theory Decoupled worldvolume theory
          %p
            On the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BLG+model"} BLG model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ABJM+model"} ABJM model
            for the
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coincident+branes"} coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            see there.
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#BaggerLambertMukhiPapageorgakis13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Bagger"}> Jonathan Bagger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Lambert"} Neil Lambert
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sunil+Mukhi"} Sunil Mukhi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantinos+Papageorgakis"} Constantinos Papageorgakis
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multiple Membranes in M-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.3546"} arXiv:1203.3546
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2013.01.006"} doi:10.1016/j.physrep.2013.01.006
          %h3#dualities Dualities
          %p
            The role of and the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            of the membrane is discussed in the following articles.
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T-duality"} T-duality
            is discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                J.G. Russo,
                %em T-duality in M-theory and supermembranes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9701188"}> arXiv:hep-th/9701188
                )
            %li
              %p
                M.P. Garcia del Moral, J.M. Pena, A. Restuccia,
                %em T-duality Invariance of the Supermembrane
                (
